    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (72.82) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) emerge as our premier offensive engines. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a high-ceiling matchup against Rocker, where a favorable park environment and a significant +13% boost from his platoon advantage elevate his output. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** is a prime start against Bassitt; despite a slightly lower base projection, the +19% SP skill adjustment\u2014reflecting a favorable matchup against the opposing starter\u2019s expected ERA of 4.91\u2014makes him a cornerstone for our runs and RBI potential. While **Gleyber Torres** (59.94) narrowly missed the \"Strong\" threshold, his role atop the order and a favorable platoon look against Newcomb provide the necessary floor to justify his inclusion.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Braden Montgomery** (39.41) and **Gavin Sheets** (39.12), both of whom fell just short of our 40.0 efficiency floor. **Braden Montgomery** was the closest to a start, but a difficult matchup against Jobe, which carried a -17% SP skill penalty, pushed him firmly into the bench category. Elsewhere, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.41) and **JJ Bleday** (48.36); while both occupy marginal starting territory, they remain in the lineup to ensure we don't bleed too many plate appearances, though their scoring is suppressed by negative platoon dynamics. \n\nFinally, a quick status check on the remaining roster: we continue to monitor the statuses of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Bryce Harper**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Luis Arraez**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Alex Freeland** for future availability. Note that **Will Smith** remains sidelined on the IL, and **Justin Crawford** is currently unavailable due to a team off-day. Given the scarcity of stolen bases in our current 5x5 format, keep a close eye on **Masyn Winn**, whose efficiency is slightly capped today by a challenging matchup against Holmes, though his elite speed remains our primary hedge against a stagnant SB category.",
